    "interpretation": [
      "Every run used the same encoded 500-packet burst, seed actors, repeat count, and packet schedule; ON artifacts report nativeCrowdReducerActive=true and OFF artifacts report false.",
      "The actor-command branch ranges do not overlap in these samples: OFF 8.914-10.585 ms; ON 6.285-8.544 ms. This supports a material actor-reducer improvement, while its 6.840 ms median still misses the 1-3 ms target.",
      "The whole-burst ranges overlap: OFF 11.721-14.840 ms; ON 12.168-14.023 ms. The 0.988 ms median regression is smaller than observed cross-process spread and does not establish that native actor reduction makes the mixed workload slower.",
      "Branch estimates are not additive: they come from separate full-buffer scans, subtract a separately timed decode pass, and exclude nonlinear effects from interleaving packet kinds, allocation, cache state, and garbage collection.",
      "Runs were grouped OFF then ON rather than randomized. Shared-host scheduling and temporal drift can affect the three-process medians. No end-to-end speed claim is made from this sample."
    ]
  },
  "retainedDecision": "Keep the production hook opt-in and keep the packed store benchmark-only. Do not expand native state ownership or port interpolation based on these results."
}
